The trick is to enchant your armour to +3 and then read a b?EA.This
will make the armour +4 or +5 (I think there is a possibility of +6
but I could be wrong).If it goes to +4, enchant up the rest of your
armour.If you _still_ have spare scrolls either use a disenchanter or
a c?EA to bring the piece of armour back down to +3.
I often trap a disenchanter in a room in the castle for this purpose.

With most weapons you can engrave a few letters to bring the weapon
down 1 enchantment (except for blunt weapons).

Thus you need never blow up your stuff by over-enchanting unless you
have so many spare scrolls that you are trying for +6 or +7 armour (I
once heard of a +10 Excalibur).

